{"acronym": "sec", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "", "description": "The Security Area is the home for working groups focused on security protocols. They provide one or more of the security services: integrity, authentication, non-repudiation, confidentiality, and access control. Since many of the security mechanisms needed to provide these security services employ cryptography, key management is also vital.\r\n\r\nThe Security Area intersects with all other IETF Areas, and the participants are frequently involved with activities in the working groups from other areas. This involvement focuses upon practical application of Security Area protocols and technologies to the protocols of other Areas.", "id": 1260, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Security Area", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1260/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2026-03-18T10:09:15Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/area/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": false}